   231	  - **An interrupted session** is a slot with a start and no end when its step resumes.
   232	    - The launcher records each session's process id and host in `launches.jsonl`.
   233	    - On resuming, a recorded process that is still alive is stopped, and its stop is recorded. Only then is the slot marked `interrupted`.
   234	    - Any output that process leaves is void.
   235	    - An interrupted session counts as a void, so it uses the single rerun. Two readers can never run for one slot.
   236	- **Validity schema** (code, fixed now), one object per question.
   237	  - **The keys, exactly:**
   238	    - `question_id`: c01 to c15, each once;
   239	    - `no_view`: boolean;
   240	    - `reference`: `text` (string), `value` (finite number or null), `items` (list of ids);
   241	    - `implied_outcome`: `text` (string), `low` and `high` (finite numbers or null), `yes_no` (boolean or null), `items` (list);
   242	    - `direction`: above, in_line, below, yes or no;
   243	    - `confidence`: high, medium or low;
   244	    - `decisive_items`: a list;
   245	    - `against`: an object with `text` (string or null) and `items` (list), or null;
   246	    - `reasoning`: a string;
   247	    - `outcome_on_due_day`: present for an event only, absent for a figure; one of that question's rung labels, or null when `no_view`.
   248	  - **When `no_view` is true,** every other field may be null or empty.
   249	  - **Otherwise:**
   250	    - `reference.text`, `implied_outcome.text` and `reasoning` are non-empty;
   251	    - a figure has `low` ≤ `high` (both numbers), `yes_no` null, and `direction` above, in_line or below;
   252	    - an event has `yes_no` a boolean, `low` and `high` null, `direction` yes or no consistent with `yes_no`, and `outcome_on_due_day` consistent
   253	      with `yes_no`;
   254	    - `decisive_items` holds 2 to 6 distinct ids;
   255	    - every item id anywhere in the object exists in the packet: in the item-list fields, and every token matching `i` followed by three digits
   256	      in the free text of `reasoning`, `text` and `why`.
   257	  - **A row whose `question_id` is outside c01 to c15** is recorded and ignored. The question it should have been is caught as missing.
   258	  - **Scale cannot be checked by code** (420 for $420bn passes). A scale slip may show as an A–B disagreement. When both readers make the same
   259	    slip, it passes unnoticed; only the signing page, which prints each range with the question's unit, can show it.
   260	  - **An invalid row** is asked again once by `templates/ask-again.md`, in a new session.
   261	    - That session gets the brief, the packet and that one question, and the template, which carries the shape additions. The template lists only
   262	      reasons from the closed set `templates/ask-again-reasons.json`.
   263	    - The reader's earlier row is not shown, so it judges afresh, as in the established Stage A ask-again.
   264	    - If the row is still invalid, the question is unresolved and goes to Alex.
   265	  - **Fewer than 2 decisive items is never asked again.** The question goes straight to unresolved, so a reader is never pressed to cite more.
   266	    More than 6, or a repeated id, is a shape error and is asked again.
   267	
   268	## 5. Reconcile (step 3)
   269	
   270	- **Agreement, by code:**
   271	  - a figure: the two closed ranges [low, high] intersect;
   272	  - an event: `outcome_on_due_day` is equal;
   273	  - both no_view: they agree, and the reference is no_view (not exercised);
   274	  - one side no_view: a disagreement.
   275	- **The proposed reference is reader B's answer** (D262).
   276	- **Disclosure: the judge was tuned to the frozen reader B's reasoning.** The Stage B judge ran poc-v108 with `judging-v7`, and D263 wrote
   277	  judging-v7's clauses from reader B's answers on this same packet. Examples are "sized from its disclosed comparable" (the credit-support
   278	  reasoning behind q09, c01 and c11), "guided growth" and discounting targets.
   279	  - A Claude-family reader of the same packet may reproduce that reasoning. Agreement between the judge and B's proposed answers is therefore not
   280	    fully independent of the judge's tuning.
   281	  - The signing page states this. The line scored against reader A is printed as prominently as the main line (§9).
   282	  - The judge's OpenAI family, shared with reader A, is not offered as a reason for B.
   283	- **Every disagreement goes to two third readers,** one of each family, inline and in the closed environments of §4.
   284	  - They see the brief, the packet, the question, and `templates/third-reader.md` with both answers as Answer 1 and Answer 2, on sides drawn by the
   285	    manifest's seed. This is the Stage A third readers' practice (`collect_readings.py disputes`). The reader output instruction is not included;
   286	    `third-reader.md` carries the shape additions and its own return line.
   287	  - **"cannot decide" must cite at least one item id.** A "neither" answer with fewer than 2 decisive items goes straight to unresolved, as in §4.
   288	  - Each rules "1", "2", **"neither"** or **"cannot decide"**. The seed's key maps "1" and "2" back to A or B.
   289	    - "Neither" carries its own answer in the §4 schema, validated by the same code.
   290	    - "Cannot decide" carries its reason with item ids. It goes to Alex like any split; it does not exclude the question.
   291	  - An invalid ruling is asked again once by `templates/third-reader-ask-again.md`, with its closed reasons.
   292	  - A missing or invalid ruling is asked again once; if still missing, the question is unresolved.
   293	- **Nothing is replaced automatically.**
   294	
   295	## 6. Alex signs (step 4)
   296	
   297	- **Who signs:** only Alex. Signing cannot be delegated (AGENTS §7.1; D592), because the council has seen the judgements. While he is inactive,
   298	  the line waits.
   299	- **The signing page** `control-reference-v1-for-signing.md` is generated by the fixed generator, in plain English. It shows:
   300	  - D660's three rules and the kept no-reference notes;
   301	  - the 15 questions, with the stripped text recorded;
   302	  - each proposed answer with its items, printed in the question's unit;
   303	  - every disagreement, with both answers and both rulings;
   304	  - every no_view, invalid or unresolved row;
   305	  - every voided output beside its replacement (§0).
   306	
   307	  It shows no judge answer and no chosen rung. The judgement-text check runs on it.
   308	- **The presenting message** is `templates/signing-summary.md`, its English and Chinese lines filled with the counts only. Claude adds no
   309	  recommendation on a disputed question, and any reply to Alex during signing quotes the page only.
   310	- **Agreed questions** (A and B agree under §5) are listed with B's answer as proposed. His one signature over the page confirms them, and he may
   311	  change any of them by the closed set below. **Disputed, invalid or unresolved questions** each need an explicit choice.
   312	- **His choices per question,** a closed set:
   313	  - a **valid** answer of A, of B or of a third reader (an invalid row cannot be picked);
   314	  - his own answer in the §4 schema, which code validates;
   315	  - **leave out**, which makes it no_view;
   316	  - **reject**, which excludes the question; his reason is recorded and its status kept.
   317	- **A disputed, invalid or unresolved question without a choice blocks the freeze.** If Alex declines to sign, nothing is scored, and that is
   318	  recorded.
   319	
   320	## 7. Freeze (step 5)
   321	
   322	- **`control-reference-v1.json`** holds:
   323	  - `reference_version: 1`;
   324	  - both readers' sha256;
   325	  - each question's source (agreed, or Alex's choice in his words);
   326	  - the stripping record;
   327	  - the label model-authored.
   328	- **Its sha** goes to `control-reference-v1.sha256`, the decision record, and a frozen-file test (`tests/test_frozen_control_reference.py`, as
   329	  `test_frozen_rulers.py`). The scorer reads the sha from that file and refuses a mismatch.
   330	- **Never edited.** A later defect becomes a dated correction record, printed with every score.
   331	
   332	## 8. Material shown (step 6, after the freeze)
   333	
   334	- **The brief.** `control-items-brief.md`, written now for review in this folder and fixed in the manifest. It is the items part of
   335	  `control-reader-brief.md` with its rule word for word: "Search the entries for the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a
   336	  related item is". The same-question and same-due parts, and the names "ruler question" and "reader B", are removed.
   337	- **The readers.** Two readers, one of each family, inline and closed as in §4, see each control's reference decisive items and the evidence
   338	  entries from `judge-inputs-v1.json`.
   339	- **The rule is unchanged:** every request on or before 2026-07-14. Its limit is disclosed: an item shown in an earlier request may be absent
   340	  from the last request whose answer is compared (`STAGE_B_READING.md`).
   341	- **Sessions.** Each reader session gets one control: its question (stripped), its reference decisive items, and its evidence entries. The keys
   342	  of a row are exactly `control`, `items` (each decisive item id mapped to shown or not_shown) and `why`. `why` may be empty only when every item
   343	  is shown.
   344	- **Disputes** go to third readers of each family, one point a session, who rule without the two answers.
   345	  - A split between the third readers is `unresolved`, reported apart from `not_shown`. A split is never asked again.
   346	  - Only an **invalid** ruling is asked again once, by `templates/items-third-ask-again.md`.
   347	- **What the readers see of each question.** The shown-check readers get each control's question from the **stripped** question file (D660:
   348	  "stripped from the rungs shown to readers").
   349	- **A failed or invalid answer** is asked again once by `templates/items-ask-again.md`, with its closed reasons; if it still fails, the control is
   350	  unresolved.
   351	- **Before scoring,** the outputs' shape and the frozen reference's sha are checked. A failure stops the scoring; it does not exclude controls.
   352	
   353	## 9. The count (step 7, `control_reference_count.py`, fixed in the manifest with its tests)
   354	
   355	**Exclusions,** each listed with its reason and never counted:
   356	- not built;
   357	- no judgement on or before 2026-07-14;
   358	- the reference is no_view, left out or rejected;
   359	- fewer than 2 decisive items;
   360	- an item not_shown;
   361	- an item unresolved, reported apart.
   362	
   363	**Agreement:**
   364	- **A figure:** the band of the last judgement's rung, [lo, hi), overlaps the reference's [low, high]. This is the frozen scorer's half-open rule
   365	  (`score_judgement.py`).
   366	- **An event:** the label of the last judgement's rung, resolved from its stored position through the question's rungs, equals the reference's
   367	  `outcome_on_due_day` (D660).
   368	- **"The last judgement"** is the one with the highest `judgement_id` on or before 2026-07-14, as in `control_theses.py` and `score_judgement.py`.
   369	- **The "fewer than 2 decisive items" exclusion** cannot fire under §4's validity rule. It is kept as a guard against a signed own-answer that
   370	  slipped past.
   371	
   372	**The verdict is D428's line:**
   373	- **MET:** at least 8 controls counted, and all but one of them agree.
   374	- **MISSED:** at least 8 counted, and two or more disagree.
   375	- **UNEXERCISED:** fewer than 8 counted. The report names each exclusion's cause.
   376	
   377	**Reported beside the verdict, never changing it (D660):**
   378	- **Null baselines.** Each is paired with the judge on its own available controls. For each, the report prints the controls it covers, the
   379	  judge's agreements there, the baseline's agreements there, and "above", "equal" or "below". A baseline available on no control prints
   380	  "unavailable".
   381	  - **Figures, lookup** (ruler-v1 §1): the rung containing `reference.value`. Unavailable when the value is null or no rung contains it.
   382	  - **Figures, middle** (D660's example): rung 3 of 5. For figures with a stated reference, the ladder puts that value in the middle range (the
   383	    ladder request, line 16). For the others it is the model's own centre, which is disclosed.
   384	  - **Events, always Still open** (D660's example). On a Yes / No event it is always No: the status quo.
   385	- **The line against reader A,** printed as prominently as the main line, with the D263 disclosure (§5) beside both: the same counted controls,
   386	  with A's answer in place of the reference.
   387	  - A's no_view, invalid or unavailable answers are not counted, and the denominator is printed.
   388	  - It is a sensitivity reading: the material shown was checked against the reference's items, not A's.
   389	- **The A–B disagreement rate.**
   390	- **Per matter:** each seed question id (q04, q07, q08, q09, q13, q16, q18) with its counted controls and agreements.
   391	
   392	## 10. Predictions, written before any reader runs
   393	
   394	- **The old reference's 8 of 15 with every item shown is a historical count, not a bound.**
   395	- **An unexercised result** may come from no_view, invalid or unresolved references, missing judgements, unresolved shown checks, or delivery. The
   396	  report names which.
   397	- **A missed result** is specific to this reference, these questions and these stored judgements.
   398	- **Most A–B disagreements will split by family.** On 9 of Stage B's 12 splits, each third reader sided with its own family's first reader. Those
   399	  splits were on judgement verdicts.
   400	
   401	## 11. What it does not measure, and its weak points
   402	
   403	- **Not measured:** whether the right questions were opened (D1); delivery beyond the shown filter (D2); the judge's daily path.
   404	- **Model-authored.** Alex's signature is the human vote, and the noise is printed.
   405	- **One stored run,** on the luna configuration's questions.
   406	  - MET shows the line met on these 15. It does not pass Stage B, which also missed the strictest last-answer reading.
   407	  - MISSED stops the line before further spend (D355).
   408	  - UNEXERCISED names its causes.
   409	- **Tuning exposure.** If a miss leads to a judge change (D263), these 15 become tuning data, and the next application must be on unseen questions.
   410	
   411	## 12. State × event
   412	
   413	| Event | What happens |
   414	|---|---|
   415	| Build refusal | The whole build stops; to the council |
   416	| A judgement-text hit in any participant-facing file | The build stops; to the council |
   417	| A stored input, template, environment or tool version differs from the manifest | The step refuses; to the council |
   418	| The manifest is re-issued after any step | Every dependent artifact (reader outputs, rulings, signature, frozen reference, shown-check outputs) is void; recorded |
   419	| A slot already has a completed or running session | Not launched again |
   420	| A session is void (closed set, §4) | Recorded; one fresh rerun; a second void makes its questions unresolved |
   421	| An interruption mid-step | The step reruns from its last completed predecessor. Outputs are written whole with their sha; a partial output is discarded and recorded |
   422	| An invalid reader row | Asked again once; if still invalid, unresolved |
   423	| A and B disagree | Two third readers |
   424	| A third reader is missing or invalid, or rules "neither" | Missing or invalid: asked again once, else unresolved. "Neither" goes to Alex |
   425	| Alex inactive | The line waits |
   426	| Alex amends | From the closed set, in his words; the page is regenerated and re-signed |
   427	| A disputed, invalid or unresolved question has no choice, or Alex declines | No freeze, nothing scored; recorded |
   428	| The signed reference or the shown-check output fails its sha or shape | Scoring stops; to the council |
   429	| A shown-check session failure or invalid answer | Asked again once, else unresolved, reported apart |
   430	| A shown-check third-reader split | Unresolved, reported apart; never asked again |
   431	| A defect after the freeze | A dated correction record |
   432	| A later run with other questions | A new gold with its own decision (AGENTS §7.1) |
   433	
   434	## 13. Sources of every rule (AGENTS §11)
   435	
   436	| Rule | Source |
   437	|---|---|
   438	| The packet as material | ruler-v1 §1; D658; D659 |
   439	| The brief byte for byte; inline; no file or command | ruler-v1 §2.1; `run_reader_codex.py` |
   440	| 2 to 6 decisive items; fewer than 2 not counted | ruler-v1 §1.5; AGENTS §4 |
   441	| Events on three outcomes; every question counts | D660; ruler-v1 §2 ("一题一个区间，每题都算") |
   442	| Stripping the quoted reference; keeping the unquoted note | D660's words |
   443	| Reader B as the proposed reference | D262 |
   444	| Third readers see both answers on the reference, and neither answer on the shown check | `collect_readings.py disputes`; `control-reader-brief.md` |
   445	| All disputes to Alex; signing his alone | D658; AGENTS §7.1; D592 |
   446	| Figure comparison, threshold, window end | D428; `control_theses.py`; `score_judgement.py` |
   447	| The baselines and their use | D660 (middle, always Still open, reported only); ruler-v1 §1 (lookup) |
   448	| Freeze, correction records, frozen-file test | ruler-v1 §2; D261; `test_frozen_rulers.py` |
   449	| Closed reader environments | D658 ("两组没参与造这个系统的审查者"); ruler-v1 §2.1 |
   450	
   451	## 14. Cost
   452	
   453	The A sessions run on the operator's Codex and the B sessions on the Claude command line. Neither is an API spend. No paid model call of the
   454	pipeline is made.
   455	
   456	## 15. Changes from version 7
   457	
   458	- **Retries are blind.** Every retry reason states a shape rule only, never the earlier answer's content. The third-reader and shown-check reason
   459	  lists are rewritten.
   460	- **The questions are checked directly:** every rendered question block must equal the stripped question file byte for byte, beside the 8-word
   461	  check.
   462	- **The shown check runs one control a session** (one point a session for its third readers), with an object parser.
   463	  - The row keys are exact, and `why` may be empty only when every item is shown.
   464	  - A third-reader split is unresolved, never asked again.
   465	  - A new ask-again text covers an invalid ruling.
   466	  - Its voided outputs are printed in the count report.
   467	- **Third readers get no reader output instruction;** `third-reader.md` carries its own. "Cannot decide" must cite items, and a "neither" answer
   468	  with fewer than 2 items is unresolved.
   469	- **Interrupted sessions:** the process id is recorded, and a live process is stopped before the rerun.
   470	- **Disclosures:**
   471	  - The judge was tuned to the frozen reader B's reasoning (D263). The line against A is printed as prominently.
   472	  - A knowledge probe shows neither reader model knows post-window facts; Claude states a June 2026 cutoff. The probe repeats before step 2.
   473	- **Claude's `thinking_tokens` system events** are allowed; they were seen in the probe.
   474	- **Schema:**
   475	  - an event's `direction` must agree with `yes_no`;
   476	  - item ids in free text are checked;
   477	  - a row outside c01 to c15 is ignored and recorded.
   478	- **The manifest** pins the imported modules.
   479	- **Figures only carry `year`.**
   480	- **The signing summary** is in plain words, with the no-view count.
   481	
   482	## 15c. Changes from version 6
   483	
   484	- **Permitted source per stage.** Reader and third-reader files are checked against the stripped question file. The removal record and the
   485	  voided outputs are permitted on the signing page only.
   486	- **The third reader may rule "cannot decide",** with its reason; the question then goes to Alex.
   487	- **The Codex environment:**
   488	  - config, skills, the absence of a global AGENTS.md and the version are pinned;
   489	  - a memory positive-control probe was run: memories on, it recalled the project; flags on, "NOTHING";
   490	  - the probe repeats before each reader step and refuses on any other reply.
   491	- **Fewer than 2 decisive items** goes straight to unresolved, never asked again. The closed reasons are adjusted to match.
   492	- **One parse shape per text:**
   493	  - the first reader session returns an array;
   494	  - ask-again and third-reader sessions return one object;
   495	  - shared shape additions in `shape-additions.md`.
   496	- **New texts:** the third-reader and shown-check ask-again texts and their closed reasons.
   497	- **An interrupted session** counts as a void.
   498	- **Small fixes:**
   499	  - readers see `year`;
   500	  - shown-check readers get the stripped question;
   501	  - the signing summary calls the baselines fixed picks.
   502	
   503	## 15b. Changes from version 5
   504	
   505	- **Every participant-facing text is written out in `templates/`,** reviewed and fixed in the manifest: the output instruction, the ask-again text
   506	  with its closed reasons, the third-reader text and the signing summary.
   507	- **The population** comes from `mapping-runs.json`'s `questions` map. Each thesis resolves to its view through `clean_ladders` in its Stage B store,
   508	  as `control_theses.py` does; the `views` map is not used. The 15 ids are listed.
   509	- **The leak check:**
   510	  - words are cut on everything that is not a letter or digit;
   511	  - the columns are `reasons`, `reference`, `implied_outcome` and `why_changed`;
   512	  - the permitted source is defined per file and includes checked session outputs and the unstripped rungs;
   513	  - the test covers reader, third-reader, signing and shown-check files with planted leaks.
   514	- **Voided outputs** are printed on the signing page beside their replacements.
   515	- **Attempts:** ask-again and rerun are their own slots.
   516	- **The user-level `CLAUDE.md` content** is checked.
   517	- **The items brief** uses c-ids, one object per control.
   518	- **The files** live under `poc/data/clean-control-reference-2026-11-17/`, and code refuses the frozen ruler's folder. The change of `kind` from
   519	  asset/theme to figure/event is stated.
   520	- **"The last judgement"** is the one with the highest `judgement_id`. The 2-item exclusion is kept as a guard.
   521	
   522	## 15a. Changes from version 4 (kept for the record)
   523	
   524	- **The leak check** is source-aware. It covers the judge's reason, reference, implied outcome and why_changed. It is tested on real inputs and on
   525	  a planted leak, and a hit stops the build.
   526	- **A manifest re-issued after any step** voids every dependent artifact, the signature and the frozen reference included.
   527	- **The reader environments are closed and pinned:**
   528	  - Codex runs with `--skip-git-repo-check`, memories off, and model and effort pinned;
   529	  - Claude runs with no settings, no MCP, no tools and no slash commands, model pinned;
   530	  - both were probed today, and each session's first event is checked against the manifest;
   531	  - the void rule is now a closed set of events;
   532	  - a slot with a completed or running session is not launched again.
   533	- **The stripping rule follows D660's words:** the two quoted forms are removed and the unquoted no-reference note is kept and disclosed. The
   534	  remainder equals `interval_text`. The facts are corrected: 3 stripped, 3 kept.
   535	- **The schema:** `outcome_on_due_day` is absent for figures and null when no_view; the required texts are non-empty; the same scale slip by both
   536	  readers is disclosed.
   537	- **Signing:** agreed questions are confirmed by his one signature; disputed, invalid or unresolved questions need an explicit choice.
   538	- **The items-only brief** is written (`control-items-brief.md`) for review.
   539	- **The "always Yes" baseline is dropped,** for lack of a source. The baselines' sources are listed.
   540	- **The c-ids follow `mapping-runs.json`'s order,** without q23.

