   226	  - for either, an unreadable log, a non-zero exit, a first event that does not match the manifest, or output that cannot be parsed.
   227	  - **Slots.** Every launch has a slot: participant, step, question set and attempt kind. The attempt kinds are `first`, `rerun-after-void` and
   228	    `ask-again-<question_id>`. Before any launch, `launches.jsonl` is read, and a slot that already has a completed or running session is not
   229	    launched again. An ask-again is its own slot, so a completed first session never blocks it.
   230	  - A void session is rerun once fresh, in its own `rerun-after-void` slot. A second void makes its questions unresolved, and they go to Alex.
   231	  - **An interrupted session** is a slot with a start and no end when its step resumes.
   232	    - The launcher records each session's process id and host in `launches.jsonl`.
   233	    - On resuming, a recorded process that is still alive is stopped, and its stop is recorded. Only then is the slot marked `interrupted`.
   234	    - Any output that process leaves is void.
   235	    - An interrupted session counts as a void, so it uses the single rerun. Two readers can never run for one slot.
   236	- **Validity schema** (code, fixed now), one object per question.
   237	  - **The keys, exactly:**
   238	    - `question_id`: c01 to c15, each once;
   239	    - `no_view`: boolean;
   240	    - `reference`: `text` (string), `value` (finite number or null), `items` (list of ids);
   241	    - `implied_outcome`: `text` (string), `low` and `high` (finite numbers or null), `yes_no` (boolean or null), `items` (list);
   242	    - `direction`: above, in_line, below, yes or no;
   243	    - `confidence`: high, medium or low;
   244	    - `decisive_items`: a list;
   245	    - `against`: an object with `text` (string or null) and `items` (list), or null;
   246	    - `reasoning`: a string;
   247	    - `outcome_on_due_day`: present for an event only, absent for a figure; one of that question's rung labels, or null when `no_view`.
   248	  - **When `no_view` is true,** every other field may be null or empty.
   249	  - **Otherwise:**
   250	    - `reference.text`, `implied_outcome.text` and `reasoning` are non-empty;
   251	    - a figure has `low` ≤ `high` (both numbers), `yes_no` null, and `direction` above, in_line or below;
   252	    - an event has `yes_no` a boolean, `low` and `high` null, `direction` yes or no consistent with `yes_no`, and `outcome_on_due_day` consistent
   253	      with `yes_no`;
   254	    - `decisive_items` holds 2 to 6 distinct ids;
   255	    - every item id anywhere in the object exists in the packet: in the item-list fields, and every token matching `i` followed by three digits
